useen & Kunstzentren","Multidisziplin\u00e4r"]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["nl","fr","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"L\u2019entrepreneuriat immigr\u00e9 bruxellois","shortdescr":"Bruxelles d\u00e9tient un nombre record d\u2019entrepreneurs, l\u2019esprit entrepreneurial traverse les rues de notre capitale. Le MigratieMuseumMigration est donc all\u00e9 \u00e0 la recherche de leurs histoires de migration et a collabor\u00e9 avec des experts afin de mettre sur pied une exposition.","longdescr":"Nous vous pr\u00e9sentons des entrepreneurs immigr\u00e9s de la premi\u00e8re et de la deuxi\u00e8me g\u00e9n\u00e9ration et des entrepreneurs dont le produit fait partie de notre m\u00e9moire collective, et cela depuis des centaines d\u2019ann\u00e9es parfois. Des personnes qui ont rendu vivant une rue, un quartier, une ville, une r\u00e9gion en cr\u00e9ant des emplois.  L\u2019exposition laisse voir \u00e0 quel point l\u2019entrepreneuriat immigr\u00e9 a donn\u00e9 forme \u00e0 Bruxelles et permet \u00e9galement de comprendre pourquoi Bruxelles compte tellement d\u2019entrepreneurs par rapport \u00e0 d\u2019autres r\u00e9gions. En effet, chaque communaut\u00e9 apporte \u00e0 Bruxelles encore plus d\u2019entrepreneurs.\r\n\u00c9videmment, cette exposition ne peut dresser le portrait de tous les entrepreneurs immigr\u00e9s de chaque communaut\u00e9 mais elle montre quand et comment l\u2019entrepreneuriat immigr\u00e9 a commenc\u00e9 et comment les initiatives entrepreneuriales au sein des diff\u00e9rentes communaut\u00e9s se sont multipli\u00e9es au fil des ann\u00e9es.","performers":"L'exposition a \u00e9t\u00e9 cr\u00e9\u00e9e avec l'aide de nombreux experts : Dr. P Jean-Philippe Van Aelbrouck, Dr. Olivier De Maret, Dr. Martin Rosenfeld et Claire Scohier (IEB), Henri Erumba, Dr. Ching Lin Pang et Franck Yiji,  Zenon Lupina, Mustafa Alperen \u00d6zdemir, et d'autres. Nous remercions aussi tout particuli\u00e8rement les entrepreneurs et les associations qui ont travaill\u00e9 avec nous.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543105"},"nl":{"name":"Entrepreneurs: Brussels migrantenondernemerschap","shortdescr":"Brussel boekt een record aan ondernemers, er is een opvallende positieve ondernemersspirit in het hoofdstedelijk gewest! Het MigratieMuseumMigration ging op zoek naar het migratieverhaal hierbij en zette samen met experts een tentoonstelling op.","longdescr":"Aan het woord zijn immigrantenondernemers van de eerste, tweede generatie en ondernemers wiens product soms al honderden jaren deel uitmaakt van ons collectief geheugen. Mensen die een straat, buurt, stad, regio energie gaven door het cre\u00ebren van jobs. De expo laat zien dat immigrantenondernemerschap Brussel vorm gegeven heeft en maakt ook begrijpelijk waarom Brussel verhoudingsgewijs zoveel ondernemers meer heeft als men vergelijkt met andere Gewesten, want elke gemeenschap bracht in Brussel steeds nieuwe ondernemers voort.\r\nUiteraard kan de expo niet al de immigrantenondernemers in beeld brengen, en ook niet het ondernemerschap van elke gemeenschap, maar ze laat wel zien wanneer en hoe het immigrantenondernemerschap begonnen is. De tentoonstelling toont hoe initiatieven van ondernemers binnen gemeenschappen zich vermenigvuldigden en dat mensen uit nieuwe gemeenschappen binnen Brussel dan op hun beurt weer nieuwe initiatieven opstarten en doorgeven.","performers":"De tentoonstelling is er gekomen met de hulp van veel experten: Dr. P Jean-Philippe Van Aelbrouck, Dr. Olivier De Maret, Dr. Martin Rosenfeld en Claire Scohier (IEB), Henri Erumba, Dr. Ching Lin Pang en Franck Yiji, Zenon Lupina, Mustafa Alperen \u00d6zdemir, en anderen. Met dank vooral ook aan de ondernemers en verenigingen die meewerkten.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/mmm.brussels","email":"museum@foyer.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":"+32 2 609 55 61","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543105"},"en":{"name":"Entrepreneurs: Brussels migrant entrepreneurship","shortdescr":"Brussels has a record number of entrepreneurs, the entrepreneurial spirit runs through the streets of our capital city. The MigratieMuseumMigration therefore went in search of migration stories and collaborated with experts to put together an exhibition.","longdescr":"We are shedding light on the first- and second-generation immigrant entrepreneurs and entrepreneurs whose products have been part of our collective memory for years, decades or centuries. People who have brought a street, a neighbourhood, a city, a region to life by creating new jobs. The exhibition shows us how immigrant entrepreneurship has shaped Brussels and it also helps us to understand why Brussels has a record number of entrepreneurs compared to other regions. \r\nIndeed, each community brings even more entrepreneurs to Brussels. Of course, this exhibition cannot portray all immigrant entrepreneurs and all entrepreneurs in each community, but it aims to pinpoint when and how immigrant entrepreneurship started and how new entrepreneurial initiatives have multiplied throughout the years.","performers":"The exhibition was created with the help of many experts: Dr. P Jean-Philippe Van Aelbrouck, Dr. Olivier De Maret, Dr. Martin Rosenfeld and Claire Scohier (IEB), Henri Erumba, Dr. Ching Lin Pang and Franck Yiji, Zenon Lupina, Mustafa Alperen \u00d6zdemir, and others. Special thanks also to the entrepreneurs and organisations who worked with us.","boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543105"},"de":{"name":"Entrepreneurs: Brussels migrantenondernemerschap","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543105"},"it":{"name":"Entrepreneurs: Brussels migrantenondernemerschap","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543105"},"sp":{"name":"Entrepreneurs: Brussels migrantenondernemerschap","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543105"},"pt":{"name":"Entrepreneurs: Brussels migrantenondernemerschap","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543105"},"cn":{"name":"Entrepreneurs: Brussels migrantenondernemerschap","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.543105"}},"place":{"id":274307,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"Aujourd'hui, plus de 180 nationalite\u0301s vivent ensemble a\u0300 Bruxelles. Le MigratieMuseumMigration raconte l\u2019histoire de la premie\u0300re ge\u0301ne\u0301ration de travailleurs immigre\u0301s invite\u0301s, des premiers arrivants au Petit Cha\u0302teau, des expatrie\u0301s, des re\u0301fugie\u0301s de guerre, des Europe\u0301ens qui se sont de\u0301place\u0301s librement au sein de l\u2019UE et de tous les autres. C\u2019est un muse\u0301e chaleureux ou\u0300 les visiteurs peuvent de\u0301couvrir la ville et la vie des autres a\u0300 travers des souvenirs, mais aussi, et avant tout, un lieu accueillant pour y partager sa propre histoire.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"Werkhuizenstraat","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Sint-Jans-Molenbeek","address_line1":"Werkhuizenstraat, 17","address_line2":"1080 Sint-Jans-Molenbeek","description_web":"Vandaag de dag wonen meer dan 180 nationaliteiten samen in Brussel. Het MigratieMuseumMigration geeft de verhalen van de eerste generatiegastarbeiders, van de vroegste bewoners van het Klein Kasteeltje, van de expats, de oorlogsvluchtelingen, de Europeanen die zich vrij bewegen binnen de EU en vele anderen een permanente thuis. Het is een warme omgeving waar bezoekers via herinneringen en kunst op ontdekking gaan in Brussel en in het leven van anderen.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"Today, more than 180 nationalities live together in Brussels. The MigratieMuseumMigration gives a permanent home to the stories of the first generation of guest workers, of the earliest inhabitants of the Petit-Cha\u0302teau, of the expats, the war refugees, the Europeans who move freely within the EU and many others. It is a warm environment where visitors can discover Brussels and the lives of others through memories and souvenirs. Above all, it is a museum with plenty of room to share your own story.","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"MigratieMuseumMigration","address_street_name":"rue des ateliers","address_street_number":"17","address_street_box":null,"email":"museum@foyer.be","website":"http:\/\/www.migratiemuseummigration.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 609 55 61","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1080","address_city":"Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","address_line1":"rue des ateliers, 17","address_line2":"1080 Molenbeek-Saint-Jean","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order"